WEBVTT

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:06.700
In the 1930s, the world of animation was dominated by the famous Walt Disney Studio.

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:12.800
It specialized in films about a mouse and his friends, fairy tales, and furry creatures of the forest.

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:15.920
But towards the end of the decade, something happened.

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:23.300
Oh yeah, what kind of a cartoon is this going to be, anyway?

00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:29.740
Well, you see, play the lead in the picture, and my name is Sammy Squirrel.

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:36.080
And the story is all about me and my cute little friends of the forest.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:38.420
Oh, brother, that, that, that.

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:48.610
And Mickey Beaver and Wallace Woodchuck and Buster Badger and Horace Hedgehog and Scotty Barney Bear and Tommy Monkey and Dorothy Duck.

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:53.640
Who would like the story anyway?

00:00:55.270 --> 00:00:59.970
The something that happened was the arrival on the scene of animation director Frederick...

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:08.090
Bean Avery, a lineal descendant of Daniel Boone and hanging judge Roy Bean, and known to his friends as Tex.

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:15.560
A shy yet jovial man, his humour was based on adult concerns.

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:19.490
Concerns that had seldom before been dealt with by the animated cartoon.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:28.010
Those of irrational fear, status, or lack of it.

00:01:35.330 --> 00:01:35.750
Paranoia.

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:47.020
Sex.

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:58.960
Or if not sex, then at least a brave stab at it.

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:04.660
Who kissed a cow?

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:12.180
Tex Avery was born on February the 26th, 1908, in Taylor, Texas,

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:13.920
the son of a lumber mill worker.

00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:16.390
He attended North Dallas High School,

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:19.090
where his talents as a cartoonist soon came to the fore.

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:22.370
He graduated high school in 1926,

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:25.610
and his drawings are a notable feature of the school yearbook.

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:37.300
A trip to Los Angeles in the late 20s as driver for a party of friends

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:39.780
resulted in Tex finding a job in the docks

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:42.660
and his friends a new driver for the Homewood Run.

00:02:43.570 --> 00:02:46.390
After trying unsuccessfully to sell comic strips to magazines,

00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:48.790
he got a job in the inking and painting department

00:02:48.790 --> 00:02:50.350
at the Walter Lantz studio

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:52.790
who were producing Oswald the Rabbit cartoons.

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:55.280
Despite losing the sight of his left eye,

00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:57.510
the innocent victim of some studio horseplay,

00:02:57.750 --> 00:02:59.970
he progressed to become an animator and finally...

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:05.880
directed two films for the studio in 1936 he landed a job as a director at warner brothers

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:11.160
animation department heading up a unit that included junior animators bob clampett and chuck jones

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:16.210
who recalls the impact of texas work and didn't take us long to realize that we were in the presence

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:22.840
of somebody who who was different at 20 years old you don't analyze things like this but but if

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:26.200
i had been capable of analyzing i would have analyzed that i was in the presence of a genius

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:28.830
and there's nothing in my lifetime

00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:29.970
I'm an observer

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:32.940
have I ever found a reason to contradict that.

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:48.600
